Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.29,0:00:06.74,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Emilia must have been talking \Nabout the Earl John Doe Ball.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.74,0:00:08.08,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,John Doe?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.47,0:00:11.25,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It implies someone of no consequence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.76,0:00:16.98,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And his is a secret ball where \Nnobles hide their faces behind masks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.98,0:00:19.73,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But why invite me to that?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.18,0:00:24.66,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Perhaps she thought it would be \Nthe best place to gather intelligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.17,0:00:28.95,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,The lowlifes who infest such balls \Nfear not even the gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.95,0:00:30.94,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I... see.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.46,0:00:35.46,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Now, you'll need a mask.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.46,0:00:38.39,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We'll be sneaking\N into my old home, Constance.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.72,0:00:40.02,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The Castiel residence?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.02,0:00:43.40,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I was a regular at those balls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.99,0:00:47.48,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Someone who knows something
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.48,0:00:51.65,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,might approach you\N if you wear my old mask.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.65,0:00:53.07,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.07,0:00:57.12,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Besides, this is a good opportunity \Nfor you as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.12,0:00:58.65,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.96,0:01:02.91,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Use your brain. \NI mean to pay off your debts, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.32,0:01:08.02,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,All the guests will be good-for-nothings \Nwith lurid secrets.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.02,0:01:11.52,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Find out what those are, \Nand take them for all they're worth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.93,0:01:14.13,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I couldn't possibly...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.70,0:01:17.93,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,No, I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.28,0:01:21.40,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I didn't get it until now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.12,0:01:24.01,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,"Be you sincere."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.51,0:01:27.51,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I've always believed \Nthat was the right thing to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.87,0:01:32.19,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,But my father was tricked, \Nand Pamela framed me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.70,0:01:35.92,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Sincerity alone won't solve anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.56,0:01:40.01,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I'll be wicked if that's what it takes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.52,0:01:41.70,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.70,0:01:44.20,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Take me to the Castiel residence.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.63,0:01:49.99,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,A Grail casting aside \Ntheir famous sincerity? What fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.53,0:03:24.86,Main - Top + Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I've yet again managed to sneak in \Nsomewhere without issue.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.46,0:03:28.00,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,But this manor is huge!\N Positively enormous.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.00,0:03:30.10,Default,Maximilian,0,0,0,,What are you doing there, girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.73,0:03:36.30,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Lady Scarlett?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.61,0:03:38.35,Default,Maximilian,0,0,0,,Did you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.35,0:03:41.92,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm, u-um, on my way \Nto the dressing room.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.92,0:03:43.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry! Please excuse me!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.67,0:03:44.80,Default,Maximilian,0,0,0,,Hey, wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.11,0:03:48.24,Default,Maximilian,0,0,0,,Have you no brain in your head?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.09,0:03:50.87,Default,Maximilian,0,0,0,,The dressing room is the other way.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.72,0:03:54.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.64,0:03:59.88,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,My brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.98,0:04:05.79,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Not much resemblance, is there?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.79,0:04:07.39,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You seem quite alike to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.89,0:04:11.81,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Your air of superiority, the way \Nyou feel entitled to call me "girl,"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.81,0:04:13.90,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,and how you insult me\N at the drop of a hat...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.90,0:04:16.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You're the first person\N to ever say as much.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.71,0:04:18.28,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Am I really?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.28,0:04:21.58,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We do have different mothers, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.43,0:04:28.88,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Constance, have you heard of \NCornelia of the Starry Crown?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.88,0:04:33.42,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Yes. The neighboring country of Faris\N was once a vast empire,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.42,0:04:37.54,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,and she was the last empress, \Nwho reigned during its fall, wasn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.54,0:04:39.56,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Yes, exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.16,0:04:46.60,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,At the time, the Faris Empire\N pursued a strategy
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.60,0:04:50.67,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,of marrying royalty from the nations\N it invaded to rule them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.31,0:04:56.29,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Then an imperial prince \Neloped with a certain lady,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.29,0:04:58.80,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,and they had a daughter,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.54,0:05:01.69,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Cornelia of the Starry Crown.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.27,0:05:09.19,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Her lineage entitled her to the crowns \Nof vassal states as numerous as the stars,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.19,0:05:11.34,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,not to mention the imperial throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.88,0:05:16.66,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Our own nation, Adelbide,\N was part of her empire back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.66,0:05:17.82,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Yes, it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.92,0:05:22.91,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,When the vassal states finally \Nrebelled and the empire fell,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.91,0:05:27.89,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,she escaped harm\Nin the neutral nation of Soldita.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.35,0:05:32.52,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Time passed, and word spread \Nthat a country girl in Soldita
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.52,0:05:36.94,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,carried the blood of \NCornelia of the Starry Crown.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.43,0:05:43.36,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Crownless Aliénore. She was my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.77,0:05:48.81,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You mean to say you're descended \Nfrom the imperial family of Faris?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.36,0:05:51.18,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Story time is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.18,0:05:53.36,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,My mask is in that suit of armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.36,0:05:54.63,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,R-Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.76,0:06:07.40,Default,Gatekeeper,0,0,0,,Your invitation?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.20,0:06:12.88,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It's in Earl John Doe's hat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.46,0:06:16.74,Default,Gatekeeper,0,0,0,,Welcome, uninvited guest.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.62,0:06:20.77,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So this...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.14,0:06:23.36,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,is the Earl John Doe Ball.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.00,0:06:29.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What {\i1}delightful{\i0} tastes they have.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.17,0:06:31.88,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Never you mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.88,0:06:34.16,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We're going straight to see our hostess.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.46,0:06:43.54,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,So it's Deborah's turn this time. \NI thought as much.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.52,0:06:45.80,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,You there.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.80,0:06:47.26,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.29,0:06:49.97,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Please, call me Eris.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.96,0:06:54.57,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,My, that brings back memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.57,0:06:57.93,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,We used to have a guest by \Nthe same name ten years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.93,0:06:58.90,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.79,0:07:02.24,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,she was a reckless girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.24,0:07:05.73,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Her head and body soon parted company.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.12,0:07:11.23,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your{\i0} head is firmly attached, I hope?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.12,0:07:19.71,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'm amazed you can eat.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.71,0:07:21.95,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I've been so tense this whole time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.95,0:07:24.49,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, this looks tasty too!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.96,0:07:29.20,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Hmm? Something smells sweet...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.20,0:07:32.08,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Why, this takes me back. That's Jane.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.08,0:07:33.23,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Jane?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.39,0:07:36.97,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Who might she be?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.55,0:07:41.36,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Miss Eris, I believe?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.60,0:07:47.85,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,That's totally Viscount Hamsworth.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.85,0:07:49.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,U-Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.61,0:07:50.60,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.60,0:07:54.60,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,We hide our true selves \Nbehind masks at this secret ball.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.87,0:07:59.14,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Please call me... Moon-Dappled Ham.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.14,0:08:01.30,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Again, you're not hiding anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.23,0:08:11.23,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,"Hide a tree in the forest," as they say.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.23,0:08:14.68,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,But what rotten wood \Nsomeone's brought tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.68,0:08:17.63,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Do you not think so, my lady?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.20,0:08:25.65,Default,Gatekeeper,0,0,0,,Run! The Security Force caught on!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.65,0:08:26.94,Default,Guests,0,0,0,,Caught on to what?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.94,0:08:27.89,Default,Guests,0,0,0,,What's going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.48,0:08:30.80,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Look at him go!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.73,0:08:34.39,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Seems I was right about those girls.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.47,0:08:39.77,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You heard what the nouveau riche hog\N said about a tree in the forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.27,0:08:44.06,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Someone was using this whole ball \Nas cover for human trafficking.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.55,0:08:46.05,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,N-No...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.05,0:08:47.53,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,No more chitchat.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.53,0:08:49.16,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You need to run.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.93,0:08:55.35,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What are you doing? Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.35,0:08:56.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,B-But...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.71,0:09:01.14,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Help!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.34,0:09:05.43,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,No one's going to help her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.43,0:09:06.70,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Not a soul!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.19,0:09:11.44,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Constance?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.65,0:09:15.44,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I remember this woman from earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.82,0:09:17.19,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,A tattoo?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.19,0:09:19.09,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You'll get caught in the raid!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.09,0:09:20.82,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Just leave her there!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.51,0:09:22.57,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Scarlett!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.53,0:09:25.08,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Sorry. I can't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.71,0:09:29.09,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Connie, you fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.58,0:09:31.83,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You'll be doomed if they catch you!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.83,0:09:34.59,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Even if you've done nothing wrong,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.59,0:09:37.35,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,they'll put you to death\N before you know it!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.35,0:09:38.90,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Scarlett!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.90,0:09:39.85,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Forgive me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.85,0:09:42.73,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,If you feel the need \Nto apologize, get running!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.73,0:09:43.72,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,You there!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.92,0:09:46.54,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.54,0:09:48.35,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,N-No!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.19,0:09:56.38,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What is {\i1}she{\i0} doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.74,0:09:59.36,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I should be asking you that, you lout!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.90,0:10:07.32,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,Who the hell are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.78,0:10:12.63,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Drawing your blade \Non an unarmed young lady?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.36,0:10:15.13,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Hardly a reasonable response.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.88,0:10:19.37,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,L-Lord Ulster!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.37,0:10:21.88,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,But she used some kind \Nof strange trickery!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.88,0:10:27.51,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Should that take precedence over \Nsaving the wounded, Jeorg Gaina?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.88,0:10:38.31,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,You again, Constance Grail?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.17,0:10:41.25,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.17,0:10:47.41,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,As a formality, did you have \Na hand in human trafficking?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.91,0:10:51.47,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I thought not.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.95,0:10:54.42,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Then I have no cause to arrest you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.34,0:10:58.67,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Still, three chance meetings must be fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.44,0:11:02.50,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Don't you think it's high time \Nyou came clean with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.16,0:11:04.67,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Scarlett...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.19,0:11:10.81,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Take them for all they're worth.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.47,0:11:15.12,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Lord Ulster was born \Nto the House of Richelieu.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.12,0:11:17.54,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,They're great nobles,\N on par with the Castiels.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.02,0:11:19.22,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,In which case...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.82,0:11:22.08,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,W-Would you care to negotiate?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.17,0:11:27.40,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Oh, of course. The Grails are in debt.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.40,0:11:29.95,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,"If you want information, pay for it"?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.95,0:11:31.95,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,He saw through me instantly!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.71,0:11:35.33,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Is that your proposal?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.33,0:11:37.01,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Er, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.01,0:11:38.96,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Well, I can't say I mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.58,0:11:44.68,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Constance Grail, are you \Nwilling to suffer scandal?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.97,0:11:48.27,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I've abandoned my sincerity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.27,0:11:50.50,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I'll take whatever life throws at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.85,0:11:52.59,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It's a bit late to worry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.59,0:11:56.28,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I see. In that case, \Nthe simplest method...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.06,0:11:58.11,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,is to get engaged.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.11,0:11:59.55,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'd like nothing better!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.36,0:12:04.31,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Good. We'll go with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.02,0:12:06.16,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Getting engaged.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.61,0:12:08.14,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wh-Wha...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.73,0:12:11.99,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.33,0:12:17.45,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,S-So, you w-want to...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.22,0:12:20.47,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,to pledge your engagement?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.47,0:12:22.72,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Yes. Please do the honors.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.15,0:12:25.27,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,W-Well, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.79,0:12:28.04,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,M-May the gods...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.04,0:12:30.78,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,b-bless your union.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.27,0:12:31.10,Main - Top + Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,How did I get into this mess?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.10,0:12:35.09,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Oh, honestly! Now you see why I avoid him!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.83,0:12:39.49,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,Now you can clear \Nthe Grail family's debts,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.99,0:12:42.49,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,and I have a pretext\N to keep an eye on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.08,0:12:47.19,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,Naturally, you'll be free to \Nannul our engagement before long.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.19,0:12:48.95,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,Still, are you certain?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.95,0:12:53.11,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,I don't see how our engagement \Nbenefits Your Lordship much.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.62,0:12:56.24,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,To tell the truth, childish as it may be,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.12,0:12:58.49,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,I don't want to marry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.99,0:13:03.01,Flashback - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,But he's certainly \Nbeen married once before.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.44,0:13:07.77,Flashback - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,To Lady Lily Orlamunde, \Nwho passed away two years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.77,0:13:12.09,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,In any case, having a fiancée \Nshould act as a repellent.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.67,0:13:16.02,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,So from my perspective, \Nour arrangement is purely beneficial.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.34,0:13:19.65,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,Now, to business.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.89,0:13:24.49,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.49,0:13:28.53,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,You want to clear Scarlett Castiel's \Nghost of her false conviction.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.91,0:13:32.92,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Really, girl. Surely you should \Nhave held {\i1}something{\i0} back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.92,0:13:35.29,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,Candidly, your story is preposterous.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.77,0:13:40.16,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,But... it's unusually \Nconsistent for a fiction.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.74,0:13:47.75,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,And the look you get sometimes \Ndoes resemble Scarlett Castiel's.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.15,0:13:50.43,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,I could almost believe you were her.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.69,0:13:56.01,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,If you want to clear her name, \Nsuit yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.42,0:14:00.80,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,She may be deceased, but your desire \Nto help others is still laudable.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.80,0:14:02.94,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,Why, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.70,0:14:04.95,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,What for?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.95,0:14:06.23,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.66,0:14:07.70,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,That aside,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.04,0:14:10.21,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,are you sure you aren't \Nstill hiding something?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.69,0:14:16.78,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.50,0:14:19.12,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,Not a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.12,0:14:20.21,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.31,0:14:24.42,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Lordship?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.79,0:14:28.72,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,Constance Grail. Or rather, Miss Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.72,0:14:30.80,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,A word of warning for your future.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.41,0:14:35.02,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,You are, well...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.13,0:14:38.30,Flashback,Randolph,0,0,0,,a rather poor liar.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.39,0:14:45.57,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,So, what are you going to do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.39,0:14:47.82,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.24,0:14:51.83,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'm sure you're through \Nhelping me, at any rate.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.83,0:14:53.33,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Huh? Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.33,0:14:56.58,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I mean, your debt troubles are over.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.09,0:15:02.47,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you laughing at?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.47,0:15:04.25,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Listen, Scarlett.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.25,0:15:07.96,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,When faced with problems\N I couldn't solve myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.96,0:15:10.46,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I was always giving them up as hopeless.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.46,0:15:13.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But deep inside, I was always shouting.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.60,0:15:15.28,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,"Someone help me!"
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.24,0:15:18.73,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,And then...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.19,0:15:20.48,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.48,0:15:21.86,Flashback,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'll help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.23,0:15:29.89,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Come to think of it, \NI've never once told you...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.90,0:15:32.72,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank you for helping me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.61,0:15:40.00,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So, now it's my turn to help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.26,0:15:43.20,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.61,0:15:48.07,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Stupid Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.94,0:15:55.77,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,That oaf Gaina can't do anything right!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.05,0:15:57.26,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.32,0:16:02.26,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Remember the human trafficking ring we\N rounded up at the old Montrose residence?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.26,0:16:06.35,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,The slavers we caught then \Ntook poison and died in jail.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.35,0:16:10.90,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,You know how quick they are to do that!\NTying them up is basic procedure!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.90,0:16:14.15,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Kyle, did their ringleader \Nhave a tattoo of the sun?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.67,0:16:17.52,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,No, and I even checked their assholes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.33,0:16:23.04,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Meaning they had no ties\N to the Daeg Gallus organization.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.37,0:16:25.62,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Or they were simply disposable.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.62,0:16:27.75,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Well, my money's on the latter.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.57,0:16:31.29,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Guess we're back\N to square one on this case.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.61,0:16:36.20,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Say, wasn't that girl at the scene again? \NConstance Grail, was it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.84,0:16:41.81,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,What now? Call her in for questioning?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.81,0:16:43.21,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,That won't be necessary.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.21,0:16:45.27,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,What, you already questioned her?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.27,0:16:47.48,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,No, we got engaged.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.94,0:16:53.13,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I'll visit the Elbaite Villa\N with her tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.13,0:16:55.57,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I expect to be back in the afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.57,0:16:58.31,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Whoa, whoa, whoa! \N{\i1}Who{\i0} got engaged to {\i1}whom{\i0}?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.91,0:17:00.58,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Who else but me...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.92,0:17:02.43,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,and Constance Grail?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.43,0:17:04.12,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.75,0:17:11.09,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,Raise your heads.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.09,0:17:12.51,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,C-Certainly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.74,0:17:17.12,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,His Lordship did say that \Nhe wanted me to meet a friend of his,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.38,0:17:21.10,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,CROWN PRINCE ENRIQUE ADELBIDE
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.12,0:17:20.49,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,but I never dreamed \Nhe meant the crown prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.09,0:17:25.56,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,And from Scarlett's perspective,\Nthis is the man who broke their betrothal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.14,0:17:30.11,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,CROWN PRINCESS CECILIA ADELBIDE
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.30,0:17:29.64,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry I'm late!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.35,0:17:33.20,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Wow, what a surprise!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.20,0:17:35.35,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,How artless! And adorable!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.35,0:17:36.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm adorable?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.60,0:17:38.10,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That wasn't a compliment.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.10,0:17:39.58,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wait, it wasn't?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.37,0:17:43.12,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Your name's Constance, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.12,0:17:45.05,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,May I call you Connie?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.05,0:17:46.37,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,O-Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.37,0:17:49.24,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,And you must call me Cess.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.24,0:17:52.21,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Surely that wouldn't be proper.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.21,0:17:55.63,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Oh, but I was born \Na viscount's daughter just like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.63,0:17:57.63,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I understand, but still...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.63,0:17:58.90,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.39,0:18:02.10,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Why don't we sit down to tea\N together sometime soon?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.10,0:18:04.16,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,You wouldn't mind, would you, Connie?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.16,0:18:05.15,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,N-Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.50,0:18:09.87,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I know he looks scary, \Nand he really {\i1}is{\i0} scary,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.87,0:18:11.60,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,but he's not a bad person.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.60,0:18:13.94,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,So don't give up on him, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.94,0:18:15.90,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, no, I mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.42,0:18:19.40,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,His Lordship scares me to death!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.40,0:18:21.59,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Wow. Just look at that face.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.59,0:18:23.66,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,What should I do? She scares me too!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.94,0:18:29.99,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.72,0:18:36.93,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,You know, Randy, picking a day I had \Nofficial commitments wasn't very nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.61,0:18:38.86,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.95,0:18:44.15,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Seeing you look so put out \Nis a rare treat, so I forgive you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.72,0:18:53.57,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I'm to receive a distinguished guest \Nfrom the south after this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.57,0:18:59.44,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,It was an honor to see you both, \Nif only for the briefest of moments.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.69,0:19:06.45,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Till next time, Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.41,0:19:08.79,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,So cold...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.97,0:19:16.95,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,That woman is as insolent as ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.95,0:19:20.85,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,Well, overlook the slight on my account.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.85,0:19:24.90,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Changing the subject, \Nhave you heard from Faris's emissary?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.59,0:19:26.72,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,Faris, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.17,0:19:28.97,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,They're a proud bunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.42,0:19:31.48,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,History is all they have to boast of.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.15,0:19:37.30,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be surprised if their economic \Nwoes are as bad as rumor paints them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.21,0:19:46.25,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,When Crown Princess Cecilia \Nfirst met Crown Prince Enrique,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.25,0:19:49.41,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,he must have still\N been engaged to Scarlett.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.30,0:19:53.69,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I always assumed that was \Nthe source of the tragedy. But now...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.79,0:19:59.50,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Tell me, Scarlett. What made you \Ndislike Princess Cecilia?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.50,0:20:01.50,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,No, it was the other way around.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.50,0:20:04.51,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That woman took a dislike to me first.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.51,0:20:05.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What? Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.22,0:20:09.93,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And it wasn't as though \Nshe disliked me in particular.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.93,0:20:12.89,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,No, "dislike" isn't quite the right word.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.21,0:20:18.10,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,She regarded everyone \Nwho entered her sight with enmity.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.34,0:20:21.40,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,If I had to put a name to it,\N it would be...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.82,0:20:23.19,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,hatred.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.60,0:20:26.90,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,If that's true,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.20,0:20:31.16,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,does it mean there's no true love\N between the couple?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.16,0:20:32.44,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,Are you lost...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.16,0:20:34.33,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,young lady?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.11,0:20:37.98,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That's King Ernst.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.71,0:20:41.43,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Royal Majesty?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.71,0:20:45.68,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,KING ERNST ADELBIDE
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.88,0:20:45.69,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,You're young Miss Grail?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.69,0:20:47.42,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, sire!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.69,0:20:51.68,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,I heard you were \Nthe second coming of Scarlett Castiel,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.68,0:20:54.72,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,but you seem a most charming young lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.75,0:21:02.06,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,Did you know the violets in our kingdom\N tend to have a reddish hue?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.55,0:21:05.31,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,There's a legend about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.53,0:21:11.91,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,A sprite that dwelt \Nin Adelbide's violets was careless.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.86,0:21:15.98,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,It drew too close to \Nthe dead burning in hell
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.98,0:21:18.03,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,and suffered horrible burns itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.10,0:21:21.84,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,What do you make of that?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.84,0:21:23.74,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,W-Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.63,0:21:28.45,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Step aside, Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.40,0:21:35.14,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Let me think...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.14,0:21:40.10,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Perhaps the flower sprite\N hoped to save the dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.10,0:21:42.26,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,Oh? What makes you say so?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.64,0:21:47.61,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,It wouldn't dare go on blooming so boldly\Nif it had anything to be ashamed of.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.22,0:21:50.99,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,I see. You do remind me of her.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.99,0:21:53.24,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Oh? Surely you jest.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.53,0:21:57.49,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I'm certain Scarlett Castiel would say...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.77,0:22:02.50,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,"The affairs of wildflowers \Nare no concern of mine."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.97,0:22:10.29,Default,Ernst,0,0,0,,Yes, that does sound like her.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.64,0:22:17.02,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I wonder what he knows about Scarlett.
